Pin the v145 toolset when building 3.10-3.14 with VS 2026

VS 2026's msbuild takes the toolset from PCbuild/python.props by
VisualStudioVersion: 3.15 maps 18.0 to v145, 3.13 and 3.14 map it to
v143, and 3.10 to 3.12 have no entry, fall through to v140 and fail with
MSB8020. v143 does not build everywhere either: the GitHub VS 2026 images
carry it only for some targets (the arm64 image has no x86 v143, and
pcbuild.proj builds _freeze_module as Win32 when the target is ARM64), so
3.13 and 3.14 fail with MSB8020 there too. v145 is the toolset every VS
2026 image ships for every host and target, and python.props documents
/p:PlatformToolset as the override, so pass it for the branches that do
not map 18.0 to it when --vs 2026 is selected.

This is what the windows-11-arm runner needs from September 2026, when
the label moves to the VS 2026 image and --vs 2022 can no longer resolve
a VS 17 installation through vswhere.
https://github.com/actions/runner-images/issues/14602

diff --git a/cpython-windows/build.py b/cpython-windows/build.py
index 0a43383..3e5b537 100644
--- a/cpython-windows/build.py
+++ b/cpython-windows/build.py
@@ -752,6 +752,7 @@ def run_msbuild(
     python_version: str,
     windows_sdk_version: str,
     freethreaded: bool,
+    msvc_version: str,
 ):
     args = [
         str(msbuild),
@@ -788,6 +789,18 @@ def run_msbuild(
     ):
         args.append("/property:UseTailCallInterp=true")
 
+    # PCbuild/python.props maps VisualStudioVersion 18.0 (VS 2026) to v145
+    # only from 3.15; 3.13 and 3.14 map it to v143 and older branches fall
+    # through to v140, MSB8020 either way on the VS 2026 images, which ship
+    # v143 for some targets only (no x86 v143 on arm64, where _freeze_module
+    # builds as Win32). Pin v145, present for every host and target there;
+    # python.props documents the override.
+    # See https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/v3.12.14/PCbuild/python.props#L9
+    if msvc_version == "2026" and python_version.startswith(
+        ("3.10", "3.11", "3.12", "3.13", "3.14")
+    ):
+        args.append("/property:PlatformToolset=v145")
+
     exec_and_log(args, str(pcbuild_path), os.environ)
 
 
@@ -1568,6 +1581,7 @@ def build_cpython(
                 python_version=python_version,
                 windows_sdk_version=windows_sdk_version,
                 freethreaded=freethreaded,
+                msvc_version=msvc_version,
             )
 
             # build-windows.py sets some environment variables which cause the
@@ -1638,6 +1652,7 @@ def build_cpython(
                 python_version=python_version,
                 windows_sdk_version=windows_sdk_version,
                 freethreaded=freethreaded,
+                msvc_version=msvc_version,
             )
             artifact_config = "PGUpdate"
 
@@ -1650,6 +1665,7 @@ def build_cpython(
                 python_version=python_version,
                 windows_sdk_version=windows_sdk_version,
                 freethreaded=freethreaded,
+                msvc_version=msvc_version,
             )
             artifact_config = "Debug" if debug else "Release"
 
